;; Each minor version's guide is built from the latest patch tag of that minor version, e.g. 0.16.2
;; for 0.16. This file overrides that source, e.g. to publish a fix made after the release.
;;
;; A key is a full version. It applies only while that version is the latest patch of its minor
;; version, so a new patch release makes the override stale, without a cleanup.
;;
;; A value is a git ref. CI fetches only branches and tags, so a commit must be reachable from one.
